							"documentation": "BUILT: written in every export, the same content either way (export_handlers.py:1733-1783). Holds: E = engine_fingerprint with git_commit, container image reference and uv_lock_sha256; D = data_batch_hash; R = data_analysis_recipe_sha256; A = t3_audit_steps_sha256; data_source_paths; software versions; engines; per-plot seeds (seeds_per_plot, seed_source_per_plot, seeds_per_layer, seeds_added_to_recipe); plot warnings; contact. PLANNED, not built as far as read: AR = audit recipe hash (D-0333 says the hash is also written in the run file), Rec = record hash, series key of every node (original and audit), one sha256 per data and recipe file, hashes of the exported files and the attrition table (all shown in DM-KEYS-HOME-AUDIT; D-0333 covers only the audit recipe hash; no ledger number found for the others: the owner to say). REMOVED: the 'skipped list' (t3_translation_skipped) is no longer written: audit steps are baked into the recipe and a step that cannot be written stops the reproducibility part with an ERROR.txt (ui_implementation_contract.md section 7.2 rule 8). Detail: DM-KEYS-HOME-AUDIT. Original box text: \"effective_run.yaml / E, D, R (+ file lists), AR, A, Rec, node keys (original and audit), file hashes + git_commit / + per-plot seeds + skipped list / ALWAYS written, identical content either way. Detail: DM-KEYS-HOME-AUDIT\"."
